/-
# Abelian groups of 2-coloured triangulations of the sphere (Kourovka Notebook Problem 17.35)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 17.35 (I. M. Wanless, N. J. Cavenagh):
suppose we have a finite two-colourable triangulation of the sphere, with triangles coloured black
or white so that no two triangles of the same colour share an edge. On each vertex we write a
generator, the generators commute, and `G_W` is the abelian group with the relations that the
generators around each white triangle add to zero; `G_B` is defined in the same way from the black
triangles. Conjecture: `G_W` is isomorphic to `G_B`.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import WantedExt.Combinatorics.SimplicialSphereShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.Combinatorics.SphereTriangulationColourGroupsKourovka17Problem35Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 17.35 (I. M.
Wanless, N. J. Cavenagh). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701337 (`KOU-17.35`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath
v1.8.0.

A finite triangulation of the sphere is the shared `FiniteSimplicialSphere 3`
(`WantedExt.Combinatorics.SimplicialSphereShared`): a finite geometric simplicial complex in `ℝ³`
whose underlying space is homeomorphic to `S²` (by Steinitz's theorem every finite simplicial
triangulation of the sphere is realizable this way). Its triangles are the faces with three
vertices. A proper colouring is `white : Finset ℝ³ → Bool` giving different colours to distinct
triangles with two common vertices. `G_W` is the free abelian group `X.K.vertices →₀ ℤ` modulo the
subgroup generated by the indicator functions of the white triangles, and `G_B` likewise.
-/

open MathlibExt.Combinatorics.SimplicialSphereShared

/-- **Triangles of a sphere triangulation.** For a finite simplicial 2-sphere $X$ in
$\mathbb{R}^3$, the triangles of $X$ are its faces with exactly three vertices, that is, its
2-dimensional faces. -/
def triangles (X : FiniteSimplicialSphere 3) : Set (Finset (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3))) :=
  {t | t ∈ X.K.faces ∧ t.card = 3}

/-- **Proper colourings of the triangles of a sphere triangulation.** Let $X$ be a finite
simplicial 2-sphere in $\mathbb{R}^3$, and let a colouring assign white or black to every finite
set of points of $\mathbb{R}^3$. The colouring is proper on $X$ if any two distinct triangles of
$X$ (faces with exactly three vertices) that have exactly two vertices in common receive different
colours. -/
def IsProperTriangleColouring (X : FiniteSimplicialSphere 3)
    (white : Finset (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3)) → Bool) : Prop :=
  ∀ t ∈ triangles X, ∀ s ∈ triangles X, t ≠ s → (t ∩ s).card = 2 → white t ≠ white s

/-- **Colour group of a 2-coloured sphere triangulation.** Let $X$ be a finite simplicial
2-sphere in $\mathbb{R}^3$, let a colouring assign white or black to every finite set of points of
$\mathbb{R}^3$, and let $c$ be one of the two colours. The colour group of $X$ for $c$ is the
abelian group generated by the vertices of $X$ with the relations $u + v + w = 0$ for each
triangle $\{u, v, w\}$ of $X$ (a face with exactly three vertices) of colour $c$; that is, the
free abelian group $\mathbb{Z}^{(V)}$ on the vertex set $V$ of $X$ modulo the subgroup generated by
the indicator functions of the triangles of $X$ of colour $c$. -/
abbrev colourGroup (X : FiniteSimplicialSphere 3)
    (white : Finset (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3)) → Bool) (c : Bool) : Type :=
  (X.K.vertices →₀ ℤ) ⧸ AddSubgroup.closure {f : X.K.vertices →₀ ℤ | ∃ t ∈ triangles X,
    white t = c ∧ ∀ v : X.K.vertices, f v = if (v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3)) ∈ t then 1 else 0}

/-- **Kourovka Problem 17.35 (statement).** The statement that for every finite simplicial
2-sphere $X$ in $\mathbb{R}^3$ and every colouring of the finite sets of points of $\mathbb{R}^3$
white or black such that any two distinct triangles of $X$ (faces with exactly three vertices)
with exactly two vertices in common receive different colours, the groups $G_W$ and $G_B$ are
isomorphic. Here $G_W$ is the abelian group generated by the vertices of $X$ with the relations
$u + v + w = 0$ for each white triangle $\{u, v, w\}$ of $X$, and $G_B$ is defined in the same way
from the black triangles. -/
def sphereTriangulationColourGroupsIso : Prop :=
  ∀ (X : FiniteSimplicialSphere 3) (white : Finset (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3)) → Bool),
    IsProperTriangleColouring X white →
      Nonempty (colourGroup X white true ≃+ colourGroup X white false)

/--
**Blackburn–McCourt theorem (Kourovka Problem 17.35).** Let $X$ be a finite simplicial 2-sphere in
$\mathbb{R}^3$, and let a colouring assign white or black to every finite set of points of
$\mathbb{R}^3$ so that any two distinct triangles of $X$ (faces with exactly three vertices) with
exactly two vertices in common receive different colours. Let $G_W$ be the abelian group generated
by the vertices of $X$ with the relations $u + v + w = 0$ for each white triangle $\{u, v, w\}$ of
$X$, and let $G_B$ be defined in the same way from the black triangles. Then $G_W$ and $G_B$ are
isomorphic.

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 17.35 (I. M.
Wanless, N. J. Cavenagh); resolution: S. R. Blackburn and T. A. McCourt, Triangulations of the
sphere, bitrades and abelian groups, Combinatorica 34 (2014), 527-546, Theorem 1 (for any finite
triangulation of the sphere with properly black-white coloured faces, A_W ≅ A_B); Kourovka Archive,
Problem 17.35 (Conjecture is proved), https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.5423.
-/
public theorem_wanted sphereTriangulationColourGroupsIso_holds : sphereTriangulationColourGroupsIso

end MathlibExt.Combinatorics.SphereTriangulationColourGroupsKourovka17Problem35Wanted
